{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "12: AI Helper chat",
  "description": "End-to-end: the in-panel assistant that grounds a question in the repo's own customization files and streams an answer from the user's Copilot license — behind a one-time disclosure gate. Every step embeds the numbered sequence diagram and points at the exact code for that step.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Step 1 — The chat webview",
      "file": "src/extension/agent-observability-vscode/src/chat/webview/chatViewProvider.ts",
      "line": 69,
      "description": "![12: AI Helper chat](.tours/diagrams/d-86.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 1 of 10 in the sequence diagram — `Dev → Chat webview: Ask a question`**\n\nThe AI Helper is a webview view. `resolveWebviewView` mounts the chat UI the user types into. It runs on the user's own GitHub Copilot license via the VS Code Language Model API."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 2 — Route the send",
      "file": "src/extension/agent-observability-vscode/src/chat/webview/chatViewProvider.ts",
      "line": 102,
      "description": "![12: AI Helper chat](.tours/diagrams/d-87.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 2 of 10 in the sequence diagram — `Chat webview → ChatViewProvider: postMessage send`**\n\nSubmitting a question posts a `{ type: 'send' }` message; `onMessage` routes it to `handleTurn(text)`. Quick-command buttons take the same path with a preset prompt."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 3 — The disclosure gate",
      "file": "src/extension/agent-observability-vscode/src/chat/webview/chatViewProvider.ts",
      "line": 132,
      "description": "![12: AI Helper chat](.tours/diagrams/d-88.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 3 of 10 in the sequence diagram — `ChatViewProvider → ChatViewProvider: ensureDisclosed() gate`**\n\n`handleTurn` first awaits `ensureDisclosed()` — a one-time consent gate explaining that the question plus selected LOCAL context is sent to the model. Declining stops the turn right here."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 4 — Build a grounded preamble",
      "file": "src/extension/agent-observability-vscode/src/chat/webview/chatViewProvider.ts",
      "line": 202,
      "description": "![12: AI Helper chat](.tours/diagrams/d-89.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 4 of 10 in the sequence diagram — `ChatViewProvider → ContextLoader: buildPreamble → loadMany()`**\n\n`buildPreamble` selects relevant customization files for the question and loads them with `contextLoader.loadMany(names)`, grounding the answer in the repo's own conventions."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 5 — Start the streaming request",
      "file": "src/extension/agent-observability-vscode/src/chat/languageModelClient.ts",
      "line": 31,
      "description": "![12: AI Helper chat](.tours/diagrams/d-90.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 5 of 10 in the sequence diagram — `ChatViewProvider → languageModelClient: streamRequest(model, messages)`**\n\n`streamRequest(model, messages, onDelta, token)` maps the assembled turns to Copilot chat messages and starts the streaming send."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 6 — Call the Language Model API",
      "file": "src/extension/agent-observability-vscode/src/chat/languageModelClient.ts",
      "line": 42,
      "description": "![12: AI Helper chat](.tours/diagrams/d-91.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 6 of 10 in the sequence diagram — `languageModelClient → Copilot model: model.sendRequest()`**\n\n`model.sendRequest(...)` calls the VS Code Language Model API. The first call may trigger VS Code's built-in per-extension Copilot consent prompt."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 7 — Stream the deltas",
      "file": "src/extension/agent-observability-vscode/src/chat/languageModelClient.ts",
      "line": 43,
      "description": "![12: AI Helper chat](.tours/diagrams/d-92.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 7 of 10 in the sequence diagram — `Copilot model → languageModelClient: streamed deltas`**\n\nThe response is consumed as an async stream — `for await (const chunk of response.text)` yields deltas as the model produces them."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 8 — Accumulate chunks",
      "file": "src/extension/agent-observability-vscode/src/chat/webview/chatViewProvider.ts",
      "line": 165,
      "description": "![12: AI Helper chat](.tours/diagrams/d-93.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 8 of 10 in the sequence diagram — `languageModelClient → ChatViewProvider: onDelta chunks`**\n\nEach delta is appended to the accumulator in the `onDelta` callback back in the provider."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 9 — Throttled HTML render",
      "file": "src/extension/agent-observability-vscode/src/chat/webview/chatViewProvider.ts",
      "line": 160,
      "description": "![12: AI Helper chat](.tours/diagrams/d-94.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 9 of 10 in the sequence diagram — `ChatViewProvider → Chat webview: assistantHtml (throttled)`**\n\nRendering is throttled: at most once per `RENDER_THROTTLE_MS`, the accumulated markdown is converted to HTML and posted as `assistantHtml`, so the bubble updates smoothly without re-rendering on every token."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 10 — Final answer",
      "file": "src/extension/agent-observability-vscode/src/chat/webview/chatViewProvider.ts",
      "line": 178,
      "description": "![12: AI Helper chat](.tours/diagrams/d-95.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 10 of 10 in the sequence diagram — `Chat webview → Dev: rendered answer`**\n\nA final render flushes the complete answer and `assistantDone` marks the turn finished. The full response shows in the webview; only the question and selected local context ever left for the model."
    }
  ]
}
